1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,496
Honey Bunny Kidz presents:

2
00:00:03,496 --> 00:00:06,450
Lulu Lamb's Sleepy Animal Stretches.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,046
It was almost bedtime.

4
00:00:11,046 --> 00:00:13,351
The moon peeked in the window,

5
00:00:13,351 --> 00:00:15,725
and the stars began to twinkle.

6
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:19,275
But Honey Bunny was still hopping!

7
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:21,625
Hop, hop, hop!

8
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:25,375
Mama, my legs are so wiggly!

9
00:00:25,725 --> 00:00:28,050
I can't stop hopping!

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,225
You had a busy, happy day, little one.

11
00:00:32,575 --> 00:00:35,925
Now your body needs help to slow down.

12
00:00:36,675 --> 00:00:40,575
What do you think helps a wiggly body feel calm?

13
00:00:40,925 --> 00:00:42,475
Hmm?

14
00:00:44,475 --> 00:00:46,508
A slow, sleepy stretch!

15
00:00:46,508 --> 00:00:48,775
And look who came to help.

16
00:00:51,425 --> 00:00:55,282
Lulu Lamb and Mimi Kitten were visiting with their mamas,

17
00:00:55,282 --> 00:00:57,725
who were having tea in the kitchen.

18
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,873
Baa! Hello, Honey!

19
00:00:59,873 --> 00:01:02,337
We know the best sleepy stretches!

20
00:01:03,087 --> 00:01:04,598
Animal stretches!

21
00:01:04,598 --> 00:01:06,715
Meow! Do you want to try?

22
00:01:07,465 --> 00:01:09,340
Yes, please!

23
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:13,148
Everybody, find a soft mat.

24
00:01:13,498 --> 00:01:15,040
Pink, green, or blue.

25
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,226
Which color mat would you pick?

26
00:01:19,226 --> 00:01:21,090
I pick the green one!

27
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,101
I'm ready!

28
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,570
First, the kitty stretch!

29
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:28,584
Get on your hands and knees,

30
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:29,883
like a kitty cat.

31
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:32,705
Now push your back up high,

32
00:01:32,705 --> 00:01:34,638
like a round, round hill.

33
00:01:34,988 --> 00:01:36,846
Up, up, up.

34
00:01:37,596 --> 00:01:40,420
Then let your tummy sink down slowly,

35
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:42,397
and look up at the stars.

36
00:01:43,147 --> 00:01:44,454
Up like a hill,

37
00:01:44,454 --> 00:01:46,197
and down like a bowl!

38
00:01:46,547 --> 00:01:48,547
That feels nice!

39
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:51,651
Let's do it three times.

40
00:01:51,651 --> 00:01:52,262
One.

41
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:54,470
Two. Three.

42
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:58,069
Can you make a kitty sound?

43
00:01:58,419 --> 00:02:00,808
What does a kitten say?

44
00:02:02,808 --> 00:02:05,138
Meow! Soft and sleepy.

45
00:02:05,138 --> 00:02:05,884
Meow.

46
00:02:08,534 --> 00:02:09,295
My turn!

47
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:11,993
This one is called the sleepy sheep.

48
00:02:12,743 --> 00:02:14,407
Sit back on your heels,

49
00:02:14,407 --> 00:02:15,751
and curl up small,

50
00:02:15,751 --> 00:02:17,542
like a soft, woolly ball.

51
00:02:18,292 --> 00:02:20,089
Rest your head down.

52
00:02:20,089 --> 00:02:21,574
Now rock gently.

53
00:02:21,924 --> 00:02:23,419
Side to side.

54
00:02:23,419 --> 00:02:24,915
Side to side.

55
00:02:25,665 --> 00:02:28,315
I'm a tiny, fluffy cloud!

56
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,774
Can you curl up small,

57
00:02:30,774 --> 00:02:32,346
like a sleepy sheep?

58
00:02:32,696 --> 00:02:34,995
Let's try together.

59
00:02:36,995 --> 00:02:39,227
Baa. So cosy.

60
00:02:41,877 --> 00:02:43,677
Hoo-hoo!

61
00:02:44,277 --> 00:02:45,845
Who says hoo-hoo,

62
00:02:45,845 --> 00:02:47,177
at the window?

63
00:02:47,527 --> 00:02:49,227
Can you guess?

64
00:02:51,227 --> 00:02:52,947
It's me, Ollie Owl!

65
00:02:52,947 --> 00:02:54,902
Good evening, friends!

66
00:02:55,252 --> 00:02:58,202
May I show you my owl stretch?

67
00:02:58,952 --> 00:03:00,920
Open your arms wide,

68
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,802
like big owl wings.

69
00:03:03,152 --> 00:03:05,126
Flap them slowly.

70
00:03:05,126 --> 00:03:06,902
Flap, and flap.

71
00:03:07,652 --> 00:03:10,327
Now turn your head gently.

72
00:03:10,677 --> 00:03:11,646
This way,

73
00:03:11,646 --> 00:03:12,939
and that way.

74
00:03:12,939 --> 00:03:14,877
Owls look all around.

75
00:03:15,627 --> 00:03:18,835
Slow wings make me feel so calm.

76
00:03:21,485 --> 00:03:22,762
Now I have one!

77
00:03:22,762 --> 00:03:24,535
It's the bunny breath!

78
00:03:25,285 --> 00:03:26,875
Bunnies sniff, sniff,

79
00:03:26,875 --> 00:03:29,060
sniff with their little noses.

80
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:31,590
Then one long breath out.

81
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:32,135
Ahh.

82
00:03:32,885 --> 00:03:34,545
Let's do it together.

83
00:03:34,545 --> 00:03:36,135
Sniff, sniff, sniff.

84
00:03:36,485 --> 00:03:38,459
And blow out slowly.

85
00:03:38,459 --> 00:03:39,060
Ahh.

86
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:43,210
How many sniffs did we do?

87
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,510
Can you count them?

88
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:48,744
Three sniffs!

89
00:03:48,744 --> 00:03:50,210
One, two, three!

90
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:54,264
My body feels soft and slow now.

91
00:03:56,914 --> 00:03:58,525
The moon smiled down,

92
00:03:58,525 --> 00:04:01,614
and the friends sang a sleepy stretch song.

93
00:04:02,364 --> 00:04:03,860
Stretch up high,

94
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:05,198
touch the sky.

95
00:04:05,548 --> 00:04:08,696
Wave hello to the moon so bright!

96
00:04:09,446 --> 00:04:10,570
Kitty arch,

97
00:04:10,570 --> 00:04:12,499
and sheep curl small.

98
00:04:13,249 --> 00:04:14,623
Owl wings flap,

99
00:04:14,623 --> 00:04:16,074
and that is all!

100
00:04:16,824 --> 00:04:19,547
Can you reach up high with us?

101
00:04:19,897 --> 00:04:22,464
Stretch, stretch, stretch!

102
00:04:24,464 --> 00:04:25,960
Stretch up high,

103
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,299
touch the sky.

104
00:04:27,649 --> 00:04:30,550
Goodnight, goodnight, sleep tight!

105
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:34,725
What a lovely, sleepy song.

106
00:04:35,075 --> 00:04:38,000
Goodnight, little stretchers.

107
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:43,170
Then Lulu and Mimi waved goodbye,

108
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:45,550
and went home with their mamas.

109
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:49,125
How does your body feel now, Honey?

110
00:04:49,875 --> 00:04:51,600
Not wiggly anymore.

111
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,775
Just sleepy.

112
00:04:53,525 --> 00:04:56,000
Which stretch did you like best?

113
00:04:56,350 --> 00:04:58,657
The kitty, the sheep, the owl,

114
00:04:58,657 --> 00:04:59,775
or the bunny?

115
00:05:01,775 --> 00:05:03,725
I liked them all!

116
00:05:04,475 --> 00:05:07,225
Let's take one more bunny breath.

117
00:05:07,575 --> 00:05:09,689
Sniff, sniff, sniff.

118
00:05:09,689 --> 00:05:10,700
And ahh.

119
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:17,200
And Honey Bunny drifted off to sleep,

120
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,475
cosy and calm.

121
00:05:19,225 --> 00:05:21,429
When your body feels wiggly,

122
00:05:21,429 --> 00:05:23,632
try a sleepy animal stretch,

123
00:05:23,632 --> 00:05:25,550
and a slow, soft breath.

124
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:30,400
Share with a friend and subscribe to Honey Bunny Kidz!

125
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,708
Goodnight, little one.

126
00:05:32,708 --> 00:05:33,801
Sweet dreams,

127
00:05:33,801 --> 00:05:36,875
and see you next time on Honey Bunny Kidz.
